In article <1992Dec22.185627.25809@ucsu.Colorado.EDU>, laruedm@ucsu.Colorado.EDU (David Larue) writes:
>*never* let your dog or cat in the room when you're trying to get ESP from
>a floating eye...my dog came in, killed the eye (while I was paralyzed),
>and ate the corpse.  So des my DOG have telepathy now?  hehe

To restate a fairly well known spoiler, throw weapons at the floating
eye and you won't get paralyzed.

When I find a floating eye, and want telepathy, first I try to keep 
my dog out of the room, and throw things at the eye until I kill it.

If my dog is already in the room, I normally don't throw anything.  I
just stand next to the eye, let the dog attack it, and hope he doesn't
eat it the very same move that he kills it.  As soon as he kills it
I move onto the corpse.

I'm not sure if the dog is really less likely to eat it in one turn
if he kills it, but I find that when I kill the eye, the dog almost
always eats it that turn, but when the dog kills it, I often have 
one turn to grab it.
